\title{quant2qual: The Automated Behavioral Narrator}
\description{
\code{quant2qual} turns numeric behavioral distributions into qualitative
case-study prose. The workflow has three steps, each a function you can run
and inspect on its own:
}
\details{
\enumerate{
\item \strong{Classify} -- \code{\link[=identify_archetype]{identify_archetype()}} standardises three behavioral
dimensions (\emph{velocity}: time, \emph{intensity}: actions, \emph{friction}: errors)
against the cohort, bands them into low / mid / high, and maps every
case onto an \code{\link[=archetype_matrix]{archetype_matrix()}} with a membership-based confidence.
\item \strong{Narrate} -- \code{\link[=generate_narrative]{generate_narrative()}} writes a clinical, UX or brief
case study for a chosen profile; \code{\link[=generate_cohort_narrative]{generate_cohort_narrative()}} writes the
cohort-level synthesis.
\item \strong{Report} -- \code{\link[=write_behavioral_report]{write_behavioral_report()}} compiles both into Markdown,
R Markdown or Quarto sources, or renders HTML and Neudata-styled PDF.
}

Everything is rule-based and local: no text leaves the machine and the same
input always produces the same prose.
}
